ds integral x; the actual response asks only for the unaffected value 2^3=8."],"questionId":"cnm_h047_q4","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_019"],"id":"cnm_h047_q4_m2","label":"Evaluate the requested power directly","methodDirectNodeIds":{"cnm_h047_q4_m2":["cnm_020","cnm_h047","cnm_h017"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_020","cnm_h047","cnm_h017","cnm_019"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A. 2900; the exact count is 2865","reason":"Zeros occur at x = 1/(kπ). The specified interval requires 1000/π < k < 10000/π, so k = 319 through 3183. There are 2865 intercepts, closest to 2900.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2003_AMC_12B_Q23","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h017","cnm_h018","cnm_h057"],"id":"count-sine-zero-indices","label":"Count the integer indices of the sine zeros","methodDirectNodeIds":{"count-sine-zero-indices":["cnm_h049","cnm_h020","cnm_h060"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h049","cnm_h020","cnm_h060","cnm_h017","cnm_h018","cnm_h057"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 2","reason":"At an intersection, (x+y)^2=k^2+2k and (x-y)^2=k^2-2k. Conversely, nonnegative values on both right sides construct real x and y. Thus intersection occurs exactly for k<=-2, k=0, or k>=2. Only k=-1 and k=1 fail, giving two integer values.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2010_AMC_12A_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_020","cnm_h017"],"id":"solution:sum-and-difference-squares:54c479547abe","label":"Use squares of the sum and difference","methodDirectNodeIds":{"sum-and-difference-squares":["cnm_148","cnm_074","cnm_h024","cnm_h020"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_148","cnm_074","cnm_h024","cnm_h020","cnm_020","cnm_h017"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":6,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B: 47","rea